to focus (the mind)\ne.g. {rig pa sgrim}:
1) the good side, the bright side of things
e.g. {bzang phyogs nas lta na} “If you look from the bright side…”
cf. {sdug phyogs}
2) good, positive
e.g. {bod nang gi 'gro ba mi'i thob thang gi gnas stangs la bzang phyogs kyi 'gyur ba gang yang mngon rgyu med pa mngon gsal/}
“Report on the lack of any perceptible positive changes in the human rights situation within Tibet”

Tibetan month, also called a Mongolian month ({hor zla}). The 12 months have many names, but the ones used by the CTA in their weekly Tibet TV news broadcasts are as follows:
1. {mchu zla ba}
2. {dbo zla ba}
3. {nag pa zla ba}
4. {sa ga zla ba}
5. {snron zla ba}
6. {chu stod zla ba}
7. {gro bzhin zla ba}
8. {khrums stod zla ba}
9. {dbyug gu zla ba}
10. {smin drug zla ba}
11. {mgo zla ba}
12. {rgyal zla ba}

a final (in sports)
+ {gnang} = to compete in a final;
e.g. {bud med sil spol rtsed 'gran mtha' ma de bal yul dang don grub gling gnyis bar gnang rgyu/}
“Team Kathmandu and Dhundupling enter women’s basket ball finals”
cf. {mtha' ma'i 'gran bsdur}

1. {dkar mdzes bod rigs rang skyong khul /} Kardze Tibetan Autonomous Prefecture, a prefecture of {si khron} Sichuan encompassing a region that is traditionally part of Kham.
(Chinese name: 甘孜县 Garze/Ganzi Prefecture)
Has 18 subdivisions:
1) {dar mdo grong khyer}
2) {lcags zam rdzong}
3) {rong brag rdzong}
4) {brgyad zur rdzong}
5) {nyag chu rdzong}
6) {rta'u rdzong}
7) {brag 'go rdzong}
8) {dkar mdzes rdzong}
9) {nyag rong rdzong}
10) {sde dge rdzong}
11) {dpal yul rdzong}
12) {ser shul rdzong}
13) {gser thar rdzong}
14) {li thang rdzong}
15) {'ba' thang rdzong}
16) {phyag 'phreng rdzong}
17) {'dab pa rdzong}
18) {sde rong rdzong}
2. Kardze County, a {rdzong} (county) within Kardze Prefecture (see point 8 above)

Autonomous Prefecture, a geographical division of China. As of June 2005, there are 30 of these, of which 10 are primarily or partly Tibetan. Of those 10, 8 are primarily Tibetan:
1. {kan lho}
2. {mtsho byang}
3. {mtsho lho}
4. {rma lho}
5. {mgo log}
6. {yul shul}
7. {dkar mdzes}
8. {bde chen}
And 2 are partly Tibetan:
1. {mtsho nub} (partly Mongolian)
2. {rnga ba} (partly Qiang)
